  "summary": "A high-volume 5/3/1-style linear progression where each day pairs a main lift for 9 sets with a secondary lift for 8 sets. Training maxes go up weekly based on how many reps you get on the heavy single.",
  "evidenceNote": "Very high volume: 17 sets of main lifts per session. On the 4-day version the bench pattern gets 26 sets a week (9 volume bench, 9 heavy bench, 8 close-grip) plus 8 OHP sets. Most sets sit well short of failure while the 1+ and final '+' sets are near-maximal. It suits intermediates coming off a novice program who can recover from long sessions. Known weaknesses: sessions are long, TM jumps based on one single can outrun real strength and lead to stalls, and accessory work is left entirely to the lifter.",
