  "schedule": "4 days a week per the spreadsheet: Monday volume bench + OHP, Tuesday squat + sumo deadlift, Thursday heavy bench + close-grip bench, Friday deadlift + front squat. Warm up to the first lift, do all its sets, then the second lift, then accessories.",
  "progression": {
    "type": "PERCENT_TM",
    "description": "Training max (TM) starts at 90% of your 1RM; the sheet rounds the TM up (CEILING) to 5 lb or 2.5 kg, and rounds every set weight (MROUND) to 5 lb or 2.5 kg. Each week, the '1+' set (95% x1+) on each T1 day sets that lift's TM change for the next week: 0-1 reps no increase; 2-3 reps +5 lb; 4-5 reps +5-10 lb; more than 5 reps +10-15 lb. The rule is the same for every lift (no upper/lower split in the source). In kg (approximate conversion, not in the source: 5 lb -> 2.5 kg, 10 lb -> 5 kg, 15 lb -> 7.5 kg): 0-1 reps +0; 2-3 reps +2.5 kg; 4-5 reps +2.5-5 kg; 6+ reps +5-7.5 kg. The bench TM is driven by Thursday's 1+ set (Monday's volume bench has no 1+ set, only a final 8+). The spreadsheet also says to increase the TM each week if you completed all the reps, and that you enter the new TM manually. T2 lifts use percentages of the related main lift's TM (OHP from OHP, sumo deadlift from deadlift, close-grip bench from bench, front squat from squat).",
    "incrementKg": {
      "upper": 2.5,
      "lower": 2.5
    },
    "deload": "No scheduled deload in the author's spreadsheet. A 0-1 rep result on the 1+ set means no TM increase that week; no further reset rule is given in the official sheet."
  },
